.SH "نام (NAME)"
timew-gaps \- display time tracking gaps
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
.nf
\fBtimew gaps\fP [\fI<range>\fP] [\fI<tag>\fP\fB...\fP]
.fi
.br
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
Displays a summary of time that is neither tracked nor excluded from tracking.
.sp
The \*(Aqreports.gaps.range\*(Aq configuration setting overrides the default date range.
The \*(Aq:blank\*(Aq hint causes only the excluded time to be shown, with no tracked time.
The default date range shown is \*(Aq:day\*(Aq.
.SH "HINTS"
.sp
Apart from range hints (see \fBtimew\-hints\fP(7)), the gaps report adheres to the following hints:
.sp
\fB:blank\fP
.RS 4
Show only the time that is excluded from tracking, without showing any tracked time.
.RE
.SH "پیکربندی (CONFIGURATION)"
.sp
\fBreports.gaps.range\fP
.RS 4
For reports that show a range of data, this setting will override the default value.
The value should be a range hint, see \fBtimew\-hints\fP(7).
.RE
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.sp
\fBtimew\-summary\fP(1)